1 Getting Started: Installation and First Speech
************************************************

This is the canonical first-use procedure for a source-checkout
installation.  It starts before Emacsvox is available, establishes an
audible acceptance checkpoint, and delays personal configuration until
an isolated session has spoken successfully.  The same chapter is
published for pre-installation web access at
<https://bartbunting.github.io/emacsvox/Installation.html>.

* Menu:

* Obtaining Emacsvox::         Obtaining Emacsvox.
* Quick Installation::         Reach an isolated first spoken session.
* Confirming First Speech::    Verify the live adapter and basic feedback.
* Recovering From No Speech::  Diagnose the boundary at which speech failed.
* Persistent Startup::         Add Emacsvox to personal configuration safely.
* Building And Testing The Speech Server::


