1.6 Building And Testing The Speech Server
==========================================

Speech-server launchers live in ‘servers/’.  Build them through the
repository-root targets above so the selected paths and staging rules
remain consistent.

   The Omnivox smoke test and its audible success condition are in *note
Selecting And Checking Omnivox::.  The following protocol-level test is
only for retained direct Tcl-compatible servers.  Run one of those
launchers from the repository root, for example:

     ./servers/espeak

   Then enter:

     q {This is a test.}
     d
     s

   The ‘q’ command queues text, ‘d’ dispatches it, and ‘s’ stops speech.
Type ‘C-d’ to close the server.  Backend-specific READMEs may provide
stronger diagnostics and should take precedence over this generic smoke
test.

   From Emacs, use ‘M-x tts-speak-version’ to verify the selected
adapter and ‘M-x tts-restart’ after changing server configuration.
Omnivox also records per-process diagnostic logs below
‘$XDG_STATE_HOME/emacsvox/omnivox’, defaulting to
‘~/.local/state/emacsvox/omnivox’; spoken text is omitted unless
explicit text logging is enabled.


